00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:24.670
I'll make up the work.

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:25.890
You're darn right you will.

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:29.340
Julia, you're one of the best writers I've ever taught.

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:31.850
And you used to love my class.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:32.890
I got to do something here.

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:35.260
Like what?

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:37.240
I'm supposed to give you detention,

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:41.680
but I think that's a waste of everybody's time.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:45.270
So I've made you an appointment with the school therapist instead.

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:46.380
What? Why?

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:50.120
Because, Julia, you're not the same person

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:52.300
who's been in my class the last two years.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:54.440
I miss that person.

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:59.180
I can't just sit back and let you disappear without a fight.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:07.900
Kirsten, don't you? Well, if you behaved yourself, if you hadn't cheated on her and lied to her,

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:12.510
then we maybe wouldn't be in this fix. You'd have somebody to take care of you, and I'd be able to

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:19.650
work on the bed. Thank God. Look, Mona, in the future, you're really going to have to let me

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:24.030
know if you're going to be late like this. I mean, I got stuff to do, and if I can't count on you to

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:28.710
be here, I mean, I mean, if you need the time, I understand, but you just really got to call first,

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:28.830
Thank you, Mr.

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:31.490
